[{"location":"#QMIdealModels","page":"Home","title":"QMIdealModels","text":"Documentation for QMIdealModels.\n\n","category":"section"},{"location":"#QMIdealModels.QMIdeal","page":"Home","title":"QMIdealModels.QMIdeal","text":"QMIdeal <: IdealModel\n\nQMIdeal(components;\nuserlocations = String[],\nreference_state = nothing,\nverbose = false,\nvib_correction=0.9546)\n\nInput parameters\n\ncomponents: Components either defined \nby name (requires name to be in the Clapeyron.jl or a custom database) or\nby SMILES via MolID\nuserlocation: path of local database or NamedTuple defining the parameters\nreference-state: see Clapeyron.jl\nvib_correction: correction factor for vibrational frequencies (see Ref. (1) for details)\n\nDescription\n\nIdeal model based on data from quantum mechanical (QM) simulations from Gond et al. (2025).\n\nModel Construction Examples\n\nusing QMIdealModels\n\nidealmodel = QMIdeal(\"water\")\nidealmodel = QMIdeal([\"water\",\"carbon dioxide\"])\n\nidealmodel = QMIdeal(MolID(\"CCCO\"))\n\nReferences\n\nD. Gond, J. Arweiler, T. Specht, H. Hasse, and F. Jirasek: CHAOS - A Consistent Large-Scale Database for Sigma-Profiles and Other Molecular Descriptors, (2025), DOI: https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.19002.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"}]
